# Vercel deploy target

Production for this repo must use the **openara** Vercel team (`izak@openara.com.au` / CLI user `izak-7900`), never `izakjosef-gmailcoms-projects` / `izakjosef@gmail.com`.

Before any `vercel deploy`, `vercel env`, or domain change:

1. Run `node scripts/assert-vercel-target.mjs` (or `npm run vercel:check`).
2. Confirm `.vercel/project.json` orgId is `team_ARCaabVk2etKS7KW82gRfPQF` (openara), not `team_Tr6MBnYJHkM0PMsGobaTtZgH`.
3. Use `--scope openara` on CLI commands.
4. Prefer `npm run deploy:prod` over bare `vercel deploy`.

Commit authors for Git-triggered deploys must be **saveaus** (GitHub repo owner linked to openara). Commits authored as Milk-asf / izakjosef@gmail.com are blocked on this project.

If the assert fails: `vercel logout && vercel login`, sign in as the openara owner, then `vercel link --yes --scope openara --project kinsa-saas`.

Committed source of truth: `vercel-target.json`.
